            "title": "Advanced Programming in OOP",
            "content": [
                "Advanced programming in OOP focuses on handling complex real-world scenarios",
                "Includes exception handling, generics, and file handling",
                "Improves robustness, flexibility, and scalability of programs",
                "Essential for building real-world applications"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Exception Handling",
            "content": [
                "Exception handling manages runtime errors in a program",
                "Prevents program crashes and ensures smooth execution",
                "An exception is an unexpected event during execution",
                "Handled using try-catch mechanism"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Why Exception Handling is Important",
            "content": [
                "Prevents sudden program termination",
                "Helps in debugging errors effectively",
                "Separates normal code from error-handling code",
                "Ensures proper resource management"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Try-Catch Block",
            "content": [
                "try block contains risky code",
                "catch block handles the exception",
                "Multiple catch blocks can be used",
                "Only first matching exception is executed"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Finally Block",
            "content": [
                "Always executes whether exception occurs or not",
                "Used to close resources like files or connections",
                "Optional but recommended",
                "Ensures cleanup operations"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "throw Keyword",
            "content": [
                "Used to manually throw an exception",
                "Defined inside method or block",
                "Used for custom error conditions",
                "Example: throw new Exception()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "throws Keyword",
            "content": [
                "Used to declare exceptions in method signature",
                "Forces caller to handle exception",
                "Does not handle exception itself",
                "Can declare multiple exceptions"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Checked vs Unchecked Exceptions",
            "content": [
                "Checked exceptions must be handled at compile-time",
                "Unchecked exceptions occur at runtime",
                "Checked: IOException, SQLException",
                "Unchecked: ArithmeticException, NullPointerException"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Custom Exceptions",
            "content": [
                "User-defined exceptions for specific scenarios",
                "Extend Exception class",
                "Provide meaningful error messages",
                "Useful for application-specific errors"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Generics",
            "content": [
                "Generics allow writing code for multiple data types",
                "Ensures type safety at compile-time",
                "Reduces need for type casting",
                "Introduced in Java 5"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Advantages of Generics",
            "content": [
                "Prevents ClassCastException",
                "Improves code reusability",
                "Provides strong type checking",
                "Eliminates explicit type casting"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Generic Classes",
            "content": [
                "Classes that work with different data types",
                "Defined using type parameter <T>",
                "Example: Box<T>",
                "Reusable for multiple data types"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Generic Methods",
            "content": [
                "Methods that can operate on different data types",
                "Defined with <T> before return type",
                "No need for method overloading",
                "Works for multiple input types"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Bounded Type Parameters",
            "content": [
                "Restrict types allowed in generics",
                "Uses extends keyword",
                "Ensures only specific class types are used",
                "Example: T extends Number"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Wildcard Types",
            "content": [
                "Represent unknown generic types using ?",
                "Provides flexibility in method parameters",
                "Two types: Upper bounded and Lower bounded",
                "Used for reusable and flexible code"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Upper vs Lower Bounded Wildcards",
            "content": [
                "? extends T allows reading but not writing",
                "? super T allows writing but restricts reading",
                "Upper bound used for processing data",
                "Lower bound used for adding data"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Raw Types and Type Erasure",
            "content": [
                "Raw types ignore generics and are unsafe",
                "Can lead to runtime errors",
                "Type erasure removes generics at compile-time",
                "Generics exist only during compilation"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "File Handling",
            "content": [
                "File handling allows reading and writing data to files",
                "Used for data storage and retrieval",
                "Supports create, read, write, delete operations",
                "Uses java.io package"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "File Class",
            "content": [
                "Represents files and directories",
                "Methods: createNewFile(), exists(), delete()",
                "Provides file information like size and path",
                "Used to manage files"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Writing Files",
            "content": [
                "FileWriter writes data to files",
                "BufferedWriter improves performance",
                "Used for efficient file writing",
                "Supports appending data"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Reading Files",
            "content": [
                "FileReader reads data from files",
                "BufferedReader improves efficiency",
                "Reads data line by line",
                "Used for file processing"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Try-With-Resources",
            "content": [
                "Automatically closes file resources",
                "Prevents resource leaks",
                "Simplifies file handling code",
                "Recommended practice in Java"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Common File Handling Issues",
            "content": [
                "FileNotFoundException when file is missing",
                "IOException for file operation errors",
                "Resource leaks if files are not closed",
                "Handled using try-catch blocks"
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "Advantages of Advanced OOP Programming",
            "content": [
